SEPIADOC LICENSE AGREEMENT
Version 1.0, October 2026

SepiaDoc is made by Mako Logics LLC, a Texas limited liability company
("Mako Logics", "we"). This agreement is between you and Mako Logics, and it
applies when you install or use SepiaDoc, including its command-line tool
(sepiadoc-cli) and its updates. If you don't agree to it, don't install or use
SepiaDoc.

In short: SepiaDoc is free for personal use at home. Businesses pay for a
low-cost Business License. Your documents stay on your computer.


1. PERSONAL USE IS FREE

You may install and use SepiaDoc free of charge, on any number of computers
you own or control, for personal, non-commercial purposes. Examples: your own
household paperwork, personal taxes, forms for your family, school work, and
applying for a job.


2. BUSINESS USE NEEDS A BUSINESS LICENSE

Any other use is "business use" and needs a paid SepiaDoc Business License from
Mako Logics, one for each person who uses SepiaDoc. Business use includes using
SepiaDoc:
  (a) at or for a company, partnership, sole proprietorship, or other business;
  (b) for work you are paid for, including freelance and contract work;
  (c) at or for a government body, school, nonprofit, or other organization.

Evaluation. A business may try SepiaDoc free of charge for 30 days before
buying. After 30 days, continued business use needs a Business License.

Business Licenses are bought from Mako Logics on the terms and at the price
shown when you buy. Contact support@sepiadoc.com.


3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

You may not:
  (a) sell, rent, lease, or charge for SepiaDoc, or include it in a product or
      service you sell;
  (b) modify SepiaDoc, or reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble it,
      except where applicable law allows it despite this restriction;
  (c) remove or change any copyright, trademark, or license notice;
  (d) distribute a modified copy of SepiaDoc or its installer.

You may give other people an unmodified copy of the official SepiaDoc
installer, free of charge. Their use is covered by this agreement.


4. YOUR DOCUMENTS AND YOUR PRIVACY

Your documents belong to you. SepiaDoc works on your computer. It does not
upload your documents, has no account, and collects no usage data. It
connects to the internet only when you press Check for updates.
Details you save in SepiaDoc (such as your name, address, and signatures) are
stored on your computer, encrypted to your Windows account.


